  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"Changes the centre of the background picture (rows 7-22, columns 4-35) to the other stored picture. Fades the sound out and in again. Toggles scene_index."},
    {"at":0,"placement":"side","text":"Asks the IRQ to fade the volume out."},
    {"at":4,"placement":"side","text":"Waits until the IRQ clears bit 7: the volume is 0."},
    {"at":17,"placement":"side","text":"scene_index = 0 or 1. The IRQ sets the background colour from $7f40,scene_index."},
    {"at":23,"placement":"side","text":"Removes the fighters: the clean background goes back into the bitmap."},
    {"at":41,"placement":"side","text":"Copies the new clean background of the fight area."},
    {"at":47,"placement":"side","text":"Asks the IRQ to fade the volume in."},
    {"at":53,"placement":"line","text":"Copies the bitmap rows 7-22, columns 4-35 to the buffer $a678-$b677 and clears them in the bitmap. Runs with all RAM ($01 = $20)."},
    {"at":60,"placement":"side","text":"First character row 7."},
    {"at":68,"placement":"side","text":"32 columns."},
    {"at":104,"placement":"line","text":"Swaps the buffer $a678-$b677 with the stored picture centre at $d000-$dfff. Then copies the buffer into the bitmap rows 7-22, columns 4-35."},
    {"at":114,"placement":"side","text":"From character row $16 (22) down to row 7."},
    {"at":118,"placement":"side","text":"Pixel lines 7 down to 0."},
    {"at":122,"placement":"side","text":"32 columns."},
    {"at":150,"placement":"line","text":"Calculates the addresses of one bitmap character and its buffer copy. Input: row_index, line_index, X = column 0-31. Output: $77 bitmap, $75 buffer, Y = line_index."},
    {"at":154,"placement":"side","text":"Bitmap row address from the table $7fce, plus $20 (4 columns)."},
    {"at":169,"placement":"side","text":"Buffer $a678 + (row - 7) * 256."},
    {"at":179,"placement":"side","text":"Adds column * 8 from the table $7f7e to both pointers."},
    {"at":214,"placement":"line","text":"Swaps the 16 pages $a678-$b677 with $d000-$dfff. The caller sets $01 = $20 so that $d000 is RAM."},
    {"at":255,"placement":"line","text":"Swaps the colours of rows 7-22, columns 4-35: screen RAM $451c with $e11c and colour RAM $d91c with $e51c."},
    {"at":271,"placement":"side","text":"16 character rows."},
    {"at":273,"placement":"side","text":"32 columns."},
    {"at":275,"placement":"side","text":"Swaps the screen RAM byte."},
    {"at":285,"placement":"side","text":"Pointers + $9400 and + $0400: the colour RAM byte and its store."},
    {"at":319,"placement":"side","text":"Screen RAM pointer + 40."},
    {"at":331,"placement":"side","text":"Store pointer + 40."}
  ],
